{"duration_api_ms":10349,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"389cb04c-cb22-41c5-87b8-0bafd7df6321","total_cost_usd":0.035248,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1760,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1058,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":159},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1760,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1058,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1760},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1058,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1760,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.035248,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":159,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"# Ticket Classification: Late Delivery with Refund Request\n\n**Fixture:** customer-support-2026-09-16-v1 · **User:** user_a\n\nThe query matches two categories. Delivery is the primary category and refund is secondary.\n\n| Category | Matched keywords | Count |\n|---|---|---|\n| `delivery` | \"delivery\", \"late\" | 2 |\n| `refund` | \"refund\" | 1 |\n\n**Why delivery is primary:** The customer's problem is the late delivery. The refund is a remedy they are asking about because of the delay. The delivery policy also says to \"check tracking status first.\" So the delivery status has to be settled before anyone can assess the refund.\n\n## Required Fields\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **category** | `delivery` (Delivery / Shipping). Secondary: `refund` (Refund / Return) |\n| **owner_team** | Logistics Support (primary). Billing Support is the conditional handoff for the refund. |\n| **priority** | P2 (same for both categories) |\n| **sla** | 1 business day (same for both categories) |\n| **next_actions** | See below |\n\n## Policy Application\n\n1. **Delivery policy:** Check tracking status first. If the delivery is late beyond the promised window, open a logistics investigation ticket and offer the customer status follow-up.\n2. **Refund policy:** Check order eligibility and payment status. If the order is eligible, route it to Billing Support for refund processing.\n\n**Important:** The policy does not say that a late delivery qualifies for a refund. The agent must not promise a refund. They should only say that eligibility will be checked.\n\n## Next Actions\n\n1. Confirm the order number and tracking status. *(Logistics Support)*\n2. Compare the tracking status with the promised delivery window.\n   - **If it is late beyond the window:** open a logistics investigation ticket.\n3. Send the customer a delivery status response. Say that their refund request has been noted and is being reviewed. Do not confirm a refund.\n4. Check refund eligibility and verify the payment transaction status.\n5. If the refund criteria are met, route to Billing Support for refund processing.\n\n## Missing Information\n\nThese facts are not in the input, and none have been assumed:\n\n- **Order number:** needed for every step.\n- **Tracking status and carrier data:** unknown.\n- **Promised delivery window:** unknown, so we cannot yet say the order is \"delayed beyond the promised window.\"\n- **Payment transaction status:** unknown.\n- **Refund eligibility criteria:** the policy says \"if eligible\" but does not define eligibility. In particular, it does not say whether a late delivery qualifies.\n- **Order history and shared context for user_a:** `shared_context` is empty.","ttft_ms":2795,"type":"result","duration_ms":10388,"uuid":"1901574e-c230-4650-816b-fb9ae63da61c","ttft_stream_ms":1325,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":1325,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
